    and D <= 2024-09-30.

rule snap_net_income_limit_100_percent_fpl_48_states_dc with provenance "Net Monthly Income Eligibility Standards (100 Percent of Poverty Level), 48 States, DC, Guam, Virgin Islands column":
the snap net income limit 100 percent fpl 48 states dc of a household is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2023-10-01 <= D
    and D <= 2024-09-30
    and the household size of the household is a number M
    and the minimum of M and 8 is a number K
    and the maximum of K and 1 is a number P
    and the snap net income limit 100 percent fpl 48 states dc table for P is an amount Q
    and the snap net income limit 100 percent fpl 48 states dc additional member is an amount R
    and a number S = M - 8
    and the maximum of S and 0 is a number T
    and N = Q + T * R.

